{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Ppqt8A8pPZ3NBpv37kDJTR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only personal productivity system whose source of truth is plain markdown files â€” task/project management plus a control surface for AI-driven \"trio\" R&D work. No database, no syncing, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty`).\n\n- **What it ships (core app):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained Python HTTP server that renders a browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reads/writes the markdown files directly, and runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task management:** Tasks live in `DASHBOARD.md`, `domains/*.md`, `INBOX.md`, etc., moving through a lifecycle (active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later / restored) with priority, energy, due-date, and notes fields â€” all editable from the GUI or CLI.\n\n- **R&D Control Surface (the system's major build effort):** A per-project \"cockpit\" that manages the **trio** workflow â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build). It has evolved through four shipped versions:\n  - **v2:** session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable pinning, an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (`pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place cached summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (port-guarded â‰  8777), Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built + merged to master 2026-06-13, 9 waves GREEN, 637 tests): lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels, one seeded terminal substrate (skill auto-loads/greets once), engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-lane doc-roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-to-lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Reliability:** A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) verifies file integrity, parses every markdown file, exercises every API endpoint, and walks the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (no live `claude`, no touching the real `:8777` service), writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Branding:** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark.\n\nIn short: it's a markdown-backed personal task dashboard that has grown a sophisticated, terminal-driven orchestration layer for running and tracking AI research/planning/build sessions per project."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"490b4cc8-bcb0-49ab-9db9-6182cac41a8d","uuid":"ddf594c5-9b7a-41ad-a3b5-9d90d4803740","request_id":"req_011Cc1hrKWxwewbh1AzarHi6"}
